    {
      "name": "validate/repeated-label-paths/first-middle-last-occurrence-indexed",
      "spec": "docs/08-conformance-and-errors.md#84-paths",
      "operation": "validate",
      "purpose": "error-case",
      "input": {
        "schema": "record Item {\n    \"sku\": string,\n}\nrecord Order {\n    \"id\": string,\n    \"item\" [1,]: Item,\n}\nroot Order\n",
        "document": {
          "edges": [
            [
              "id",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": "string",
                  "value": "A-1"
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              "item",
              {
                "edges": [
                  [
                    "sku",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "integer",
                        "value": 1
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              "item",
              {
                "edges": [
                  [
                    "sku",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "string",
                        "value": "ok"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              "item",
              {
                "edges": [
                  [
                    "sku",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "integer",
                        "value": 2
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              "item",
              {
                "edges": [
                  [
                    "sku",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "string",
                        "value": "ok"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              "item",
              {
                "edges": [
                  [
                    "sku",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "integer",
                        "value": 3
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "diagnostics": [
          {
            "path": "$.item[0].sku",
            "code": "validate.type-mismatch"
          },
          {
            "path": "$.item[2].sku",
            "code": "validate.type-mismatch"
          },
          {
            "path": "$.item[4].sku",
            "code": "validate.type-mismatch"
          }
        ]
      },
      "comment": "E-10: `item` occurs five times in the root node, so every occurrence is indexed, the first included. Occurrences 0, 2 and 4 carry an integer `sku` where the schema declares string; 1 and 3 are valid. Expected paths: the first `$.item[0].sku` (the case the pseudocode used to leave unindexed), the middle `$.item[2].sku`, the last `$.item[4].sku`. `id` occurs once and is never indexed."
    },
    {
      "name": "validate/repeated-label-paths/single-occurrence-label-has-no-index",
      "spec": "docs/08-conformance-and-errors.md#84-paths",
      "operation": "validate",
      "purpose": "error-case",
      "input": {
        "schema": "record Item {\n    \"sku\": string,\n}\nrecord Order {\n    \"id\": string,\n    \"item\" [1,]: Item,\n}\nroot Order\n",
        "document": {
          "edges": [
            [
              "id",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": "string",
                  "value": "A-1"
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              "item",
              {
                "edges": [
                  [
                    "sku",
                    {
                      "scalar": {
                        "kind": "integer",
                        "value": 1
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "diagnostics": [
          {
            "path": "$.item.sku",
            "code": "validate.type-mismatch"
          }
        ]
      },
      "comment": "E-10: `item` occurs exactly once in the root node, so its path carries no index even though the schema declares it repeatable ([1,]). The index depends on how many times the label occurs in the document node, not on the declared cardinality. Expected `$.item.sku`, not `$.item[0].sku`."
    },
    {
      "name": "validate/repeated-label-paths/repeated-undeclared-field-indexed",
      "spec": "docs/08-conformance-and-errors.md#84-paths",
      "operation": "validate",
      "purpose": "error-case",
      "input": {
        "schema": "record R {\n    \"a\": string,\n}\nroot R\n",
        "document": {
          "edges": [
            [
              "a",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": "string",
                  "value": "x"
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              "extra",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": "integer",
                  "value": 1
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              "extra",
              {
                "scalar": {
                  "kind": "integer",
                  "value": 2
                }
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": false,
        "diagnostics": [
          {
            "path": "$.extra[0]",
            "code": "validate.unexpected-field"
          },
          {
            "path": "$.extra[1]",
            "code": "validate.unexpected-field"
          }
        ]
      },
      "comment": "E-10 applies to an edge the schema does not declare as it does to a declared one: `extra` occurs twice, so each unexpected-field diagnostic is indexed, `$.extra[0]` and `$.extra[1]`."
    },
    {
